ibrary.org】\nL41:   * 【12†Blog†libwww.freelibrary.org】\nL42: \nL43:   * 【15†Find】\nL44:   * 【10†Explore†libwww.freelibrary.org】\nL45:   * 【11†Ask†libwww.freelibrary.org】\nL46: # Find\nL47: \nL48:   1. 【16†Catalog Home】\nL49:   2. 【17†The man from the future :】\nL50: \nL51: 【18† †media.freelibrary.org】\nL52: \nL53: ###  The man from the future : the visionary life of John von Neumann  by 【19† Bhattacharya, Ananyo. 】\nL54: \nL55: Overall Rating:  【59†Image: Star Rating】 【60†Image: Star Rating】 【61†Image: Star Rating】 【62†Image: Star Rating】 【63†Image: Star Rating】\nL56: \nL57: Your Rating:   【4† Log in to rate. 】\nL58: #####  Book\nL59: \"The smartphones in our pockets and computers like brains. The vagaries of game theory and evolutionary biology. Nuclear weapons and self-replicating spacecrafts. All bear the fingerprints of one remarkable, yet largely overlooked, man: John von Neumann. Born in Budapest at the turn of the last century, von Neumann is one of the most influential scientists to have ever lived. A child prodigy, he mastered calculus by the age of eight, and in high school made lasting contributions to mathematics.\nL60: In Germany, where he helped lay the foundations of quantum mechanics, and later at Princeton, von Neumann's colleagues believed he had the fastest brain on the planet-bar none.\nL61: He was instrumental in the Manhattan Project and the design of the atom bomb; he helped formulate the bedrock of Cold War geopolitics and modern economic theory; he created the first ever programmable digital computer; he prophesized the potential of nanotechnology; and, from his deathbed, he expounded on the limits of brains and computers-and how they might be overcome.\nL62: Taking us on an astonishing journey, Ananyo Bhattacharya explores how a combination of genius and unique historical circumstance allowed a single man to sweep through a stunningly diverse array of fields, sparking revolutions wherever he went. The Man from the Future is an insightful and thrilling intellectual biography of the visionary thinker who shaped our century.\"--\nL63:  Saved in:\nL64: \nL65:   * 【20† Cite this】\nL66:   * 【21† Text this】\nL67:   * 【22† Email this】\nL68:   *\nL69: \nL70: 【23† Place Hold 】\nL71: \nL72: 【24† Add to My Lists 】\nL73: \nL74: Total Copies: 3\nL75: Available: 【25† 3 】\nL76: Holds: 0\nL77: #### Description\nL78: \nL79:   * Published:  New York : W.W. Norton & Company, 2022\nL80: \nL81:   * ISBN:  9781324003991 (hardcover) :, 1324003995\nL82:   * Format:  Book\nL83:   * Language:  English\nL84:   * Edition:  First American edition.\nL85:   * Subjects:\nL86:     * 【26†Von Neumann, John,】 > 【27†1903-1957.】\nL87:     * 【28†Mathematicians】 > 【29†Hungary】 > 【30†Biography.】\nL88:     * 【28†Mathematicians】 > 【31†United States】 > 【32†Biography.】\nL89:   * Physical Description:  368 pages ; cm.\nL90:   * Bibliography:  Includes bibliographical references and index.\nL91: \nL92:   * Tags:   No Tags, Be the first to tag this record!  【33†Add Tag】\nL93: \nL94:   *  Awards:\nL95: \nL96:   *  About the Author:\nL97: \nL98: * * *\nL99: #### Holdings\nL100: \nL101: 3 Available\nL102: \nL103:   Library:  Call Number:  Material:  Shelf Location:  Due Date:  Notes:\nL104: 【34†Parkway Central Library 】  NEW BOOK  Adult Paperback  Science and Wellness Department\nL105: 【35†Philadelphia City Institute 】  510.92 V896B  Adult Hardback  Adult Department\nL106: 【36†Roxborough Library 】  510.92 V896B  Adult Hardback  Biographies\nL107: \nL108: * * *\nL109: #### Table of Contents\nL110: \nL111:   1. Introduction: Who was John von Neumann?\nL112:   2. Made in Budapest\nL113:   3. To infinity and beyond\nL114:   4. The quantum evangelist\nL115:   5. Project Y and the super\nL116:   6. The convoluted birth of the modern computer\nL117:   7. A theory of games\nL118:   8. The think tank by the sea\nL119:   9. The rise of the replicators\nL120:   10. Epilogue: The man from which future?\nL121: \nL122: * * *\nL123: \nL124: #### Reader Comments\nL125